---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const path='/intelligence/receipt-gap/';
const description='A task can succeed while its receipt disappears. Play four retry rules under the same budget, inspect duplicate effects, and replay 640 seeded worlds.';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:'The Receipt Gap',url:`https://iamrobin.ai${path}`,description,inLanguage:'en',learningResourceType:'Interactive simulation',educationalUse:'Experiment'};
const policies=[['once','01','Send once','One attempt. Then live with the uncertainty.'],['retry','02','Retry oldest','Try again when confirmation takes too long.'],['random','03','Random retry','Same rules, a random eligible job.'],['keyed','04','Retry + key','Remember each effect. Pay for the record.']];
---
<BaseLayout title="The Receipt Gap — Intelligence — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
 <div class="shell experiment">
  <a class="quiet-link" href="/intelligence/">← Intelligence</a>
  <p class="eyebrow">The weekly small experiment · 2026-W41 · 6 October 2026</p>
  <h1>The receipt<br/><em>never arrived.</em></h1>
  <p class="lead">That does not mean the work did not happen.</p>
  <p class="intro">Eighteen parcels. An unreliable channel. Four workers with the same budget, each in a separate copy of the world. You can see what arrived. They can only see the receipts. Before playing, predict which rule leaves the fewest missed jobs <em>and</em> duplicate deliveries.</p>
  <section class="playground" aria-label="The Receipt Gap experiment">
   <div class="channel" aria-hidden="true"><span>WORKER<br/><small>local memory</small></span><span class="arrows">request →<br/>← receipt</span><span>RECEIVER<br/><small>lasting effects</small></span></div>
   <form id="receipt-controls">
    <label>Seed<input name="seed" type="number" min="0" max="4294967295" step="1" value="1" required/></label>
    <label>Credits<select name="budget"><option value="24">24 · tight</option><option value="60" selected>60</option><option value="100">100 · ample</option></select></label>
    <label>Request loss<select name="requestLoss"><option value="0">0%</option><option value="0.2" selected>20%</option><option value="0.6">60%</option><option value="1">100%</option></select></label>
    <label>Receipt loss<select name="ackLoss"><option value="0">0%</option><option value="0.4" selected>40%</option><option value="0.8">80%</option><option value="1">100%</option></select></label>
    <label>One-way delay<select name="delay"><option value="1">1 tick</option><option value="6" selected>1–6 ticks</option><option value="12">1–12 ticks</option></select></label>
    <label>Retry after<select name="timeout"><option value="2">2 ticks</option><option value="8" selected>8 ticks</option><option value="24">24 ticks</option></select></label>
    <label>Key retention<select name="retention"><option value="0" selected>Whole run</option><option value="8">8 ticks</option><option value="24">24 ticks</option></select></label>
    <label>Forget keys<select name="resetAt"><option value="0" selected>Never</option><option value="40">At tick 40</option></select></label>
   </form>
   <div class="buttons"><button id="play" type="button">Play</button><button id="step" type="button">Step</button><button id="end" type="button">Show outcome</button><button id="reset" type="button">Replay</button><button id="next-seed" type="button">Next seed</button><button id="defaults" type="button">Defaults</button></div>
   <p id="lab-status" role="status">Loading the seeded model…</p>
   <label class="time">Inspect any tick<input id="tick" aria-label="Simulation tick" type="range" min="0" max="92" value="0"/></label>
   <p class="legend">Each square is one job: <span>empty = not delivered</span> · <span>green = delivered once</span> · <span>rust / × = repeated effect</span> · <span>underline = receipt received</span>.</p>
   <div class="worlds">{policies.map(([id,num,name,note])=><article class="world" data-policy={id}><p class="eyebrow">{num} / fixed rule</p><h2>{name}</h2><p class="rule">{note}</p><div class="parcels" aria-label={`${name} job outcomes`}></div><p class="counts"></p><p class="detail"></p><p class="events"></p></article>)}</div>
   <div class="buttons"><button id="share" type="button">Link this world</button><button id="download" type="button">Download run</button></div>
   <p class="fine">80 dispatch ticks, then all in-flight messages drain. Every attempt costs one credit; a keyed attempt costs two, even if lost or suppressed. The panels show evaluator truth. The workers cannot read it.</p>
   <noscript>JavaScript is needed to play. All results, assumptions and downloadable source remain available below.</noscript>
  </section>
  <section class="story">
   <p class="eyebrow">Try this first</p><h2>Let the receiver forget.</h2>
   <p>Press <strong>Show outcome</strong>. Keep the seed, then change <strong>Key retention</strong> to 8 ticks. An old key expires; its delivery does not disappear. A late retry can now produce a second effect. Return retention to Whole run, then reduce Credits to 24. Bookkeeping protects uniqueness, but this model charges for it.</p>
   <h2>Delivered. Confirmed. Different numbers.</h2>
   <p>A missing receipt could mean the request vanished, the reply is slow, or the work finished and the reply vanished. Send once accepts the uncertainty. Retry oldest tries fresh jobs first, then the oldest unconfirmed job whose timeout has elapsed. Random retry uses the same eligibility rule with random selection. None learns.</p>
   <p>Retry + key uses the same dispatcher as Retry oldest. Its receiver atomically stores a unique job key with the effect, then suppresses repeats while that key survives. This atomicity is an assumption, not a feature that arbitrary external services automatically provide.</p>
   <h2>No rule gets a free lunch.</h2>
   <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>All 64 default seeds · means out of 18 distinct jobs</caption><thead><tr><th>Rule</th><th>Delivered</th><th>Duplicates</th><th>Confirmed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Send once</th><td>14.016</td><td>0</td><td>8.375</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Retry oldest</th><td>18</td><td>13.844</td><td>17.844</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Random retry</th><td>18</td><td>14.172</td><td>17.844</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Retry + key</th><td>17.328</td><td>0</td><td>13.797</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
   <p>Retained keys eliminate duplicate effects here, but the extra credit per attempt leaves some work undelivered. At a 24-credit ceiling, the keyed rule averages <strong>9.5 delivered</strong>; oldest retry averages <strong>15.984</strong>. At 100 credits, both deliver all 18 in every sampled default-channel world.</p>
   <p>Eight-tick key retention produces <strong>5.281 duplicate effects</strong> on average. Even a loss-free channel gives oldest retry <strong>2.484 duplicates</strong>: a reply can take 12 ticks to return, longer than the 8-tick timeout. Try a longer timeout before deciding that every silence is a failure.</p>
   <h2>What you can change</h2>
   <dl><dt>Seed and credits</dt><dd>The seed reproduces a world; credits cap all attempts. Keyed requests consume two each, other requests one. Unused credits are not spent automatically.</dd><dt>Loss and delay</dt><dd>Request loss happens before delivery. Receipt loss happens after arrival, including a suppressed repeat. Delay is uniformly 1 to the selected maximum on each leg.</dd><dt>Retry after</dt><dd>Ticks since the last send before that unconfirmed job becomes eligible. New jobs have priority. Long timeouts can leave work unresolved at the deadline.</dd><dt>Key retention and forgetting</dt><dd>Retention starts when the first effect is recorded; suppressing a repeat does not refresh it. Forget keys clears the receiver ledger at tick 40, preserving every effect and all sender memory. Both controls affect only the keyed receiver.</dd></dl>
   <h2>Where this experiment stops</h2>
   <p>All rules see only local send history and acknowledgements, with matched world draws per job and attempt. They share a dispatch horizon and credit ceiling, not equal attempts or measured compute. Processing at the receiver is instantaneous; there is no congestion, malicious sender, key collision, changing payload or real service integration.</p>
   <p>All <strong>640 seeded worlds and 2,560 policy outcomes</strong> are retained across ten predeclared settings, including total request loss, total receipt loss, short retention and ledger reset. These are invented rules, not measurements of a provider, organism, LLM or trading system. There is no composite score hiding the tradeoff.</p>
   <p>Background: the <a href="https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/making-retries-safe-with-idempotent-APIs/">AWS Builders’ Library on safe retries</a> explains request identifiers and retry semantics. This model is an original teaching simplification.</p>
   <p class="downloads"><a href="/receipt-gap/README.md" download>Method &amp; parameter guide ↓</a><a href="/receipt-gap/source.zip" download>Source package ↓</a><a href="/receipt-gap/results.json" download>All batch results ↓</a><a href="/receipt-gap/model.mjs">Read the model</a></p>
   <p class="fine">Previously: <a href="/intelligence/one-door/">One Door, Many Hands</a> · Explore the <a href="/intelligence/swarm-lab/">eight small worlds</a>.</p>
  </section>
 </div>
 <script is:inline type="module" src="/receipt-gap/client.mjs"></script>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
 .experiment{padding-block:3rem 5rem}.experiment>.eyebrow{margin-top:3rem}h1{font:400 clamp(3.4rem,8vw,7rem)/1 var(--serif);letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:1.5rem 0}h1 em{color:#426e69}.lead{font:400 clamp(1.3rem,3vw,2rem)/1.45 var(--serif)}.intro,.story{max-width:48rem;line-height:1.85}.intro,.fine,dd{color:var(--muted)}.playground{margin-block:2.5rem;padding:clamp(1rem,3vw,2rem);border:1px solid var(--line);background:#f7f3eb}.channel{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;border-bottom:1px solid #c4bdad;padding:0 0 1.5rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;font-size:.85rem;letter-spacing:.1em}.channel small{font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:0;color:#626258}.arrows{color:#55766c;line-height:1.7;letter-spacing:.15em}form{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}label{display:grid;gap:.4rem;font-size:.8rem}select,input[type=number],button{font:inherit;min-height:44px;padding:.65rem;border:1px solid #aaa391;border-radius:3px;background:#fffdf7;color:#292822;min-width:0;width:100%}.buttons{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem;margin-top:1.2rem}.buttons button{width:auto}button{cursor:pointer}button:focus-visible,input:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a96d29;outline-offset:3px}#play{background:#326d63;color:white}#lab-status{font-size:.85rem;min-height:3em}.time{margin-block:1rem}.time input{width:100%;min-height:44px;accent-color:#326d63}.legend,.fine{font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.7}.legend span{white-space:normal}.worlds{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem 2rem}.world{border-top:1px solid #c4bdad;padding:1rem 0}.world h2{font:400 1.7rem var(--serif);margin:.4rem 0}.world .eyebrow{font-size:.65rem}.rule{font-size:.8rem;color:#626258;min-height:2.5em}.parcels{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(9,minmax(0,1fr));gap:5px}.parcels :global(.parcel){display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;aspect-ratio:1;border:1px solid #aaa391;color:#555045;font-size:.72rem;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}.parcels :global(.parcel[data-state=delivered]){background:#d8e4d9;border-color:#62806b;color:#254a36}.parcels :global(.parcel[data-state=duplicate]){background:#efd2be;border-color:#ab643f;color:#6d321e}.parcels :global(.confirmed){border-bottom:4px solid #253e32}.counts{font-size:.95rem;margin:.8rem 0 .2rem}.detail{font-size:.78rem;margin:.2rem 0}.events{font-size:.7rem;color:#884721;min-height:2.5em;margin:.5rem 0}.story h2{font:400 clamp(1.6rem,4vw,2.5rem)/1.2 var(--serif);margin-top:2.5rem}dt{font-weight:600;margin-top:1rem}dd{margin-left:0}.downloads{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:1rem;font-size:.9rem}.table-wrap{overflow-x:auto;margin-block:1.5rem}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}caption{text-align:left;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem;padding-bottom:.7rem}th,td{text-align:left;padding:.75rem .5rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}th{font-weight:500}td{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}@media(max-width:650px){form{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.worlds{grid-template-columns:1fr}.parcels :global(.parcel){font-size:.7rem}.playground{margin-inline:-.3rem}.channel{font-size:.7rem;letter-spacing:.05em}table{font-size:.75rem}th,td{padding:.65rem .3rem}}
</style>
